    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc9e94c7_901bf6ef",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T19:33:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this be set only for modules with such need defined in Android.bp? Most rustc invocations do not need it.\nFor implementation, it would be nice to generalize this and allow any env variable-value pair to be specified in Android.bp and defined for rustc. Also when necessarily use a name different from OUT_DIR.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bde9aaf_3ab73e7f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T20:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OUT_DIR is where most Rust crates expect generated code to reside. Do we have any external/ crates currently that use a different environment variable for their generated source code?",
      "parentUuid": "fc9e94c7_901bf6ef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a09c021a_c4b8bdcf",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T22:32:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes OUT_DIR\u003dout is Rust convention, but not every Rust crate needs/uses it. So I\u0027m thinking not to define OUT_DIR for every rustc issued by .bp files.\nIf we follow Rust convention, \u0027out\u0027 seems to be a better name than \u0027gen\u0027. Just in case for Android projects not using Cargo.toml and for any reason not OUT_DIR convention, they might like a different name or multiple \"include\" directories for sources from different code generators.",
      "parentUuid": "6bde9aaf_3ab73e7f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6c21ccb_fca18756",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-15T18:24:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I only append OUT_DIR now when there is generated source. As OUT_DIR is the Rust convention and this is primarily meant to support external/ (discussed a bit further in our design doc). I don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth the added complexity at this time to support alternatives to OUT_DIR until we have a use case for it.\n\nI\u0027ve switched where the generated source is copied to from \u0027\u003cmodule_intermediates\u003e/gen\u0027 to \u0027\u003cmodule_intermediates\u003e/out\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "a09c021a_c4b8bdcf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "225425b1_ff9d2746",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T19:33:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not? We could have many prebuilt libraries and some could benefit from some simple code generator. For example, some Rust cargo build generates \"version\" files to be included. Such code generator could be written in simple script and output used in compilation of other prebuilt libraries.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
