      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T21:35:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible for multiple generated sources to collide here?  Can you use the whole genSrc path?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b903a0cc_0eaeb557",
        "filename": "rust/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115178
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-15T17:34:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible if multiple source providers produce output with the same name/stem value. In practice though we shouldn\u0027t run into this as the generated source must match the dependent source\u0027s expected output name, e.g.\n\n include!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), \"/bindings.rs\"));\n\nThis leads to why using the whole genSrc path wouldn\u0027t work -- we\u0027re constrained by what the dependent source expects the path to be. We can add support for a relative path within this directory if we find it\u0027s necessary, but we think most usage in the Rust community assumes the generated source is in the OUT_DIR root.\n\nNevertheless I added a check here to error out if there\u0027s a collision to avoid hard-to-debug issues.",
      "parentUuid": "ca1bbe87_ba896ec3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 225,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "418910c10fdb200e33e9add41d03b44e42bb18bb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
